WEBCLUSTER <-> DXSPIDER PROTOCOL
IMPLEMENTATION SPECIFICATION
Version: 1

======================================================================
1. PURPOSE
======================================================================

WebCluster (WC) maintains a single technical TCP connection to DXSpider
(DXS). Web users do not create an individual TCP connection or DXChannel
per user.

All WC users are multiplexed over a single technical #WEB-n connection.

Server:        docker-3
Host:          127.0.0.1
Port:          27754/TCP
Technical channel: #WEB-n
Version:       1

General scheme:

WC    --->    DXS     Technical connection request
WC    <---    DXS     #WEB-n assignment

WC    --->    DXS     JSON requests
WC    <---    DXS     JSON responses

WC    <---    DXS     HUMAN feed
WC    <---    DXS     RBN feed
WC    <---    DXS     ANN feed


======================================================================
2. PROTOCOL LAYERS
======================================================================

The connection uses two layers:

1. DXSpider / IntMsg transport
2. WebCluster protocol in JSON

The A, C, I, D, X, R and N prefixes belong to the DXSpider
IntMsg/Web transport layer.

The content located after the "|" character belongs to the WebCluster
protocol.

Example:

I#WEB-1|{"type":"user_add",...}
^^^^^^^^ ^
IntMsg   WebCluster JSON

Meaning used by this integration:

A
    WC    --->    DXS
    Initial request for a technical Web connection.

C
    WC    <---    DXS
    Assignment of the #WEB-n identifier.

I
    WC    --->    DXS
    Input/request sent to the #WEB-n channel.

D
    WC    <---    DXS
    Normal channel output:
    - startup text before HELLO
    - JSON responses after HELLO

X
    WC    <---    DXS
    HUMAN spot feed.

R
    WC    <---    DXS
    RBN feed.

N
    WC    <---    DXS
    ANN feed.


======================================================================
3. CONNECTION ESTABLISHMENT
======================================================================

The connection does NOT start by sending JSON.

WC    --->    DXS
TCP connect to 127.0.0.1:27754

WC    --->    DXS
A#WEB|webcluster enhanced

WC    <---    DXS
C#WEB-n

Example:
C#WEB-1

DXSpider may then send normal startup text:

WC    <---    DXS
D#WEB-n|<startup text>

WC must wait until the final DXSpider prompt is received, for example:

WC    <---    DXS
D#WEB-n|... dxspider >

Only then does WC send HELLO.


======================================================================
4. WC ---> DXS    hello
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"hello","role":"webcluster","version":1}

Fields:

type
    Value: "hello"

role
    Value: "webcluster"

version
    WebCluster protocol version.
    Current value: 1


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"hello","role":"webcluster","version":1,"status":"ok"}

Known error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"hello","role":"webcluster","status":"error","error":"unsupported_version","supported":[1]}

Known errors:

unsupported_version

WC must only consider the connection to be in READY state when it
receives:

type   = hello
role   = webcluster
status = ok


======================================================================
5. READY STATE
======================================================================

After a successful HELLO, the following requests may be sent:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"user_add",...}
I#WEB-n|{"type":"user_del",...}
I#WEB-n|{"type":"spot",...}
I#WEB-n|{"type":"ann",...}
I#WEB-n|{"type":"feed",...}

Responses:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response",...}

Common response field:

action
    Action to which the response belongs:
    user_add | user_del | spot | ann | feed

Received feeds:

X#WEB-n|{"type":"spot","payload":"<payload>"}
R#WEB-n|{"type":"rbn","payload":"<payload>"}
N#WEB-n|{"type":"ann","payload":"<payload>"}

The exact payload definition for spot, rbn and ann will be documented
separately.

The goal is that, after the "|" character, every WebCluster protocol
message is valid JSON.


======================================================================
6. WC ---> DXS    user_add
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"user_add","id":<id>,"call":"<user_call>","ip":"<user_ip>","authenticated":<true|false>}

Fields:

type
    Value: "user_add"

id
    Request identifier.

call
    Effective user callsign.
    It may include an SSID.

ip
    Real IP address of the user connected to WebCluster.

authenticated
    true
        The user has been authenticated by WebCluster.

    false
        The user is a guest/not authenticated.

IMPORTANT:

authenticated does NOT modify:

    DXUser.registered
    password
    privilege level


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"ok","action":"user_add","call":"<user_call>","ip":"<user_ip>","authenticated":<0|1>}

Generic error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"user_add","call":"<user_call>","error":"<error>"}

Known errors:

invalid_call
invalid_ip
bad_ip
already_owned
already_connected
locked_out
not_user
too_many_connections
route_add_failed

Meaning of important errors:

already_owned
    The CALL already belongs to this same #WEB-n connection.

    To change authenticated:
        USER_DEL
        USER_ADD

already_connected
    The CALL is already connected or present directly in DXSpider.

    WC MUST NOT replace or disconnect that session.

    Recommended policy:
        try an available SSID between -90 and -99


======================================================================
7. WC ---> DXS    user_del
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"user_del","id":<id>,"call":"<user_call>"}

Fields:

type
    Value: "user_del"

id
    Request identifier.

call
    User previously associated with this #WEB-n.


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"ok","action":"user_del","call":"<user_call>"}

Generic error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"user_del","call":"<user_call>","error":"<error>"}

Known errors:

invalid_call
not_owned

not_owned
    The CALL does not currently belong to this #WEB-n connection.

NOTE:

If the WebCluster TCP connection is lost abruptly, DXSpider
automatically removes the presences owned by that #WEB-n.


======================================================================
8. WC ---> DXS    spot
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"spot","id":<id>,"call":"<user_call>","freq":"<frequency>","dxcall":"<dx_call>","comment":"<comment>"}

Fields:

type
    Value: "spot"

id
    Request identifier.

call
    WC user originating the spot.

freq
    Spot frequency.

dxcall
    Announced DX callsign.

comment
    Spot comment.


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"ok","action":"spot","call":"<user_call>","result":"processed"}

Generic error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"spot","call":"<user_call>","error":"<error>"}

Known errors:

invalid_call
not_owned
not_authenticated
not_present
user_not_found
not_user
invalid_ip
bad_arguments
internal_error

A rejection from the standard handler may also be returned:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"rejected","action":"spot","call":"<user_call>","messages":[<messages>]}


======================================================================
9. WC ---> DXS    ann
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"ann","id":<id>,"call":"<user_call>","scope":"<scope>","text":"<text>"}

Fields:

type
    Value: "ann"

id
    Request identifier.

call
    WC user originating the announcement.

scope
    Announcement scope.

    Values:
        local
        full
        sysop

    If omitted:
        local

text
    Announcement text.


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"ok","action":"ann","call":"<user_call>","scope":"<scope>","result":"processed"}

Generic error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"ann","call":"<user_call>","error":"<error>"}

Known errors:

invalid_call
not_owned
not_authenticated
not_present
user_not_found
not_user
invalid_ip
bad_arguments
internal_error

A rejection from the standard handler may also be returned:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"rejected","action":"ann","call":"<user_call>","scope":"<scope>","messages":[<messages>]}


======================================================================
10. WC ---> DXS    feed
======================================================================

Format:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"feed","id":<id>,"human":<true|false>,"rbn":<true|false>,"ann":<true|false>}

Fields:

type
    Value: "feed"

id
    Request identifier.

human
    true  = enable HUMAN feed
    false = disable HUMAN feed

rbn
    true  = enable RBN feed
    false = disable RBN feed

ann
    true  = enable ANN feed
    false = disable ANN feed

human, rbn and ann are independent and optional.

Status query:

I#WEB-n|{"type":"feed","id":<id>}


WC    <---    DXS    Response

OK response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"ok","action":"feed","human":<0|1>,"rbn":<0|1>,"ann":<0|1>}

Generic error response:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"feed","error":"<error>"}

Known errors:

user_not_found
bad_arguments


======================================================================
11. GENERAL PROTOCOL ERRORS
======================================================================

Known errors:

invalid_json
missing_id
unknown_type
unsupported_version

General format when an id is available:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","id":<id>,"status":"error","action":"<operation>","error":"<error>"}

When an id cannot be obtained:

D#WEB-n|{"type":"response","status":"error","error":"invalid_json"}


======================================================================
12. DXS ---> WC    FEEDS
======================================================================

For now, only the outer structure is defined.
The exact payload content is not yet defined.

WC    <---    DXS    HUMAN SPOT

X#WEB-n|{"type":"spot","payload":"<payload>"}

WC    <---    DXS    RBN

R#WEB-n|{"type":"rbn","payload":"<payload>"}

WC    <---    DXS    ANN

N#WEB-n|{"type":"ann","payload":"<payload>"}


======================================================================
13. ASYNCHRONOUS RESPONSES
======================================================================

Responses must not be correlated by receive order.

While WC is waiting for a D#WEB-n|JSON response, it may receive:

X#WEB-n|...
R#WEB-n|...
N#WEB-n|...

WC must correlate responses using id.


======================================================================
14. RECOMMENDED STATE MACHINE
======================================================================

DISCONNECTED
    |
    | TCP connect
    v

TCP_CONNECTED
    |
    | A#WEB|webcluster enhanced
    v

WAIT_ASSIGNMENT
    |
    | C#WEB-n
    v

WAIT_STARTUP_PROMPT
    |
    | D#WEB-n|... dxspider >
    v

SEND_HELLO
    |
    | I#WEB-n|{"type":"hello",...}
    v

WAIT_HELLO_OK
    |
    | D#WEB-n|{"type":"hello",...,"status":"ok"}
    v

READY
    |
    +-- USER_ADD
    +-- USER_DEL
    +-- SPOT
    +-- ANN
    +-- FEED
    |
    +-- receives asynchronous SPOT/RBN/ANN feeds
    |
    X TCP connection lost
    v

DISCONNECTED


======================================================================
15. TEST UTILITY
======================================================================

Utility:
    wc-test.pl

Server:
    docker-3

It must be executed from inside the DXSpider container.

Default values:
    DXSPIDER_CLUSTER_ADDR = 127.0.0.1
    DXSPIDER_CLUSTER_PORT = 27754

Example:
    cd /spider/local
    ./wc-test.pl

IMPORTANT:

The "raw" command in wc-test.pl is NOT part of the protocol.

Example entered by the operator:
    raw {"type":"feed","id":<id>}

What wc-test.pl actually transmits:
    I#WEB-n|{"type":"feed","id":<id>}


======================================================================
16. RULES FOR THE WC DEVELOPER
======================================================================

1. Connect to 127.0.0.1:27754/TCP.

2. After the TCP connection is established, send:
       A#WEB|webcluster enhanced

3. Wait for:
       C#WEB-n

4. Store #WEB-n as the identifier of the current technical connection.

5. Wait until channel startup is complete and the following prompt
   appears:
       dxspider >

6. Send HELLO.

7. Do not consider the connection READY until HELLO status=ok is
   received.

8. Once READY, send JSON requests using:
       I#WEB-n|

9. Correlate responses using id.

10. Process X/R/N feeds asynchronously.

11. USER_ADD must contain the user's real IP address.

12. authenticated comes exclusively from the WC authentication system.

13. Do not synchronize:
       password
       registered
       privilege level

14. On already_owned:
       USER_DEL
       USER_ADD
    if authenticated must be changed.

15. On already_connected:
       do not modify the existing DXS session
       preferably try an SSID from -90 to -99

16. After TCP connection loss:
       discard all local ownership associated with that #WEB-n
       rebuild it after establishing a new connection.


